  "body": "A substantial 1,118m² freehold landholding with a comfortable home and exciting potential for the future.\r\n\r\nTucked privately away from the road, this generous St Heliers property combines space, privacy and flexibility. Whether you're looking for a family home, an opportunity to renovate and add value, or a substantial site for future possibilities, there's plenty to appreciate.\r\n\r\nWell-presented and ready to move into, the 1960s home offers three bedrooms, two generous living areas, an enclosed conservatory, one bathroom and a separate toilet. Timber floors add warmth and character, while a heat pump provides year-round comfort.\r\n\r\nDownstairs, a spacious rumpus offers flexibility for teenagers, hobbies or working from home, complemented by excellent storage, a freestanding double garage and generous off-street parking.\r\n\r\nOutside, the expansive, easy-rise lawn and established boundaries create a private setting for children, pets and entertaining, with room to explore adding a swimming pool.\r\n\r\nLooking ahead, you could renovate and enhance the existing home, explore building a new residence or investigate development opportunities under the Residential – Mixed Housing Suburban zoning. An indicative two-home concept illustrates one possibility, with scope to investigate further residential potential.\r\n\r\nProperty highlights:\r\n\r\n• 1,118m² freehold rear site\r\n\r\n• Well-presented 1960s home, approximately 170m²\r\n\r\n• Three bedrooms, two living areas and conservatory\r\n\r\n• One bathroom, separate WC and large downstairs rumpus\r\n\r\n• Excellent storage, double garage and additional parking\r\n\r\n• Expansive lawn with potential for a swimming pool\r\n\r\n• Residential – Mixed Housing Suburban zoning\r\n\r\n• Indicative two-home concept available\r\n\r\nWithin easy reach of St Heliers Village, the waterfront, highly regarded local schools and parks, this is an opportunity to secure space and flexibility in an established neighbourhood.\r\n\r\nMove in, make it your own or plan for what comes next. Come and experience the property for yourself.\r\n\r\nThe concept is indicative and unconsented. Any development or swimming pool is subject to Council approval and buyer due diligence, including planning, access, infrastructure and engineering requirements.\r\n\r\nSee interactive features for this property on barfoot.co.nz. Click the \"View office website\" link at the bottom of this page.",
